    "video_id": "bys8JCRuiXw"
   },
   {
    "context": "John 17, 17. Sanctify them by your truth. Your word is truth. In this passage, Jesus is praying to God the Father and asks God to sanctify or to separate his people by his truth. Starting with truth just feels a little insidious. Actually, uncovering truth should be a lifelong venture where you explore the world and uncover different ideas, and your concept of truth should evolve over time. Now, of course, an insular religion doesn't exactly want you doing that, which is why I could see it opening this extended metaphor by trying to rein in the idea of truth.",
    "dist": 0.4291,
    "occurrence_id": 4506,
    "published_at": "2024-03-07T21:00:06Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 265.28,
    "title": "The Armor of God is Stupid",
    "video_id": "3F_IZAOnqBA"
   },
   {
    "context": "And it seems to me that if we are to present Christianity to thinking men and women in such a culture, it's absolutely vital that we be able to give reasons for thinking that it's really the truth.",
    "dist": 0.4324,
    "occurrence_id": 19758,
    "published_at": "2014-12-22T15:04:16Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 61.92,
    "title": "What is the Importance of Scholarship in the Christian World?",
    "video_id": "IS020H72Qq0"
   },
   {
    "context": "Now, is there any truth to this? I would honestly have to say yes, a little. Christianity indeed depends on sheltering people and keeping their thought processes looped into prepackaged arguments and statements of dogma, and mere exposure to contrary ideas, properly considered, will almost always erode at their faith.",
    "dist": 0.4338,
    "occurrence_id": 38810,
